================================================================================
                  Code Defects Identified from Specification Theorems
              Sparse Post-Quantum Ratchet (SPQR) — Formal Verification Audit
================================================================================

METHODOLOGY
  • 221 Lean spec files under Spqr/Specs/ surveyed
  • Preconditions/postconditions cross-referenced against Rust src/ and sorted-vec 0.8.6
  • All referenced theorems compile (lake build); 28 defects identified in Rust source

─── HIGH SEVERITY ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  #1  Unvalidated from_pb → panics from corrupted state blobs
      next.len()≠32, prev.len()%36≠0, prev too large for ctr — all assumed by
      specs (NextKeyInternal, Get, Gc) but never checked in ChainEpochDirection::from_pb.
      Fix: validate and return Err(StateDecode).

  #24 Unauthenticated Ct2Sampled→KeysUnsampled epoch advance
      A single 4-byte forged message [1,2,1,0] permanently deadlocks both parties.
      recv_next_epoch consults neither MAC nor Authenticator.
      Fix: require MAC verification before epoch state transition.

─── MEDIUM SEVERITY ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  #2  u32 overflow in KeyHistory::get (at + max_ooo wraps at u32::MAX)
      Fix: use checked_add / saturating_add.

  #3  u64→usize truncation on 32-bit targets (chain trim_size)
      Fix: guard with explicit range check or use u64 throughout.

  #19 Chunk replacement poisoning persists through into_pb/from_pb
      SortedSet::push replaces on duplicate x; attacker chunk overwrites honest
      point → permanent decoder stall. Fix: reset decoder on MAC failure.

  #25 Epoch-0 chain key emitted without any authentication
      recv at epoch 0 returns key from initial_state; no MAC ever runs.
      Fix: reject epoch 0 in recv or require authentication gate.

  #28 Unvalidated ChainParams overflow (max_ooo ≥ 390,451,572)
      Release builds silently wrap; key storage inverts meaning.
      Fix: validate params in initial_state.

─── LOW SEVERITY ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  #4  hax_lib::assume! guards erased at runtime (multiple locations)
  #5  SortedSet::push comment contradicts actual replacement semantics
  #6  Encoder u32→u16 chunk-index truncation after 65,535 chunks
  #7  PolyDecoder::is_complete never set → redundant reconstruction attempts
  #8  usize overflow in trim_size on 32-bit (max_ooo ≥ 390M)
  #9  VecDeque IntoIter model unsound (FunsExternal.lean)
  #10 Source comment says "discard new" but code replaces old point
  #11-18 Various spec-assumption gaps (polynomial, authenticator, round-robin)
  #20 MapCollectBridge sorry → axiom gap in point_at_spec
  #21 Chain::from_pb missing next_root/links/send_epoch validation
  #22 Authenticator::from_pb admits empty root_key/mac_key
  #23 RoundRobinEncoder panics on empty input (test-only)
  #26-27 recv_key epoch-1 indexing, state-blob injection edge cases

─── CLASSIFICATION SUMMARY ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  Category                          Count   Remote?
  Unvalidated deserialization        12      No (state-blob injection required)
  Integer overflow / truncation       5      No
  Silent semantic corruption          4      No
  Protocol-level DoS                  3      Auth peer / forged message
  Spec model gaps                     4      N/A (proof infrastructure)

  CWE mapping: CWE-20 (input validation), CWE-190 (integer overflow),
               CWE-502 (deserialization), CWE-345 (insufficient auth)

─── KEY TAKEAWAY ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  The Lean specification theorems mechanically surface every invariant the Rust
  code fails to establish. All 28 defects exist because from_pb / recv accept
  inputs violating preconditions that specs must assume. The V1 protocol's
  MAC-before-commit pattern prevents remote exploitation of most findings, but
  SPQR's own API boundary is unsound without the proposed validation fixes.

